From: Adriel Santos <adriel@adriel.eu>
Subject: [PATCH] ath11k: tear NSS offload down after the crash-path IRQ quiesce

The NSS series inserts ath11k_nss_teardown() at the top of
ath11k_core_reconfigure_on_crash(). The same function disables the host
datapath/CE interrupts on the firmware crash path further down, so the
offload was released while ring and CE handlers could still run. Move
the teardown after the quiesce.

Taken from https://github.com/ADCDS/openwrt-xiaomi-ax3000t-rd03v2
(999-998-rd03v2-nss-teardown-after-irq-quiesce); the nss.c half of it is
already in this tree.

Signed-off-by: Stanislaw Pal <kuncy7@gmail.com>

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.c
@@ -2397,10 +2397,15 @@
 
 	mutex_lock(&ab->core_lock);
 
+	ath11k_thermal_unregister(ab);
+	/* Reset already disables these IRQs before the power cycle. */
+	if (!ab->is_reset) {
+		ath11k_hif_irq_disable(ab);
+		ath11k_hif_ce_irq_disable(ab);
+	}
 	ath11k_nss_teardown(ab);
 	ab->nss.enabled = false;
 
-	ath11k_thermal_unregister(ab);
 	ath11k_dp_pdev_free(ab);
 	ath11k_spectral_deinit(ab);
 	ath11k_ce_cleanup_pipes(ab);
